@startuml shape
!theme plain
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam nodesep 14
skinparam ranksep 45
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

title The shape of it: four ways in, one of them through the gateway

header
<b>THE TOP-LEVEL PICTURE, AND NOTHING ELSE.</b>  Every service and every message type: <b>services.puml</b>.
Only the <b>control</b> path is brokered. Realtime, bulk and admin traffic reach their service directly,
so the gateway is never in the media path and cannot be its bottleneck.
Rationale: <b>ARCHITECTURE.md</b>.   Shard keys: <b>scaling.puml</b>.   Gateway parts: <b>gateway-internals.puml</b>.
endheader

actor "Mumble client\n«legacy or Fancy»" as client #E3F2FD
actor "**operator**" as oper #F3E5F5

component "**gateway**\nTLS · framing · limits\n**single writer per client socket**" as gw #FFE9D6

component "**21 services**, tiered\nessential · core · optional\n«gRPC, no client reaches them directly»" as svc #FAFAFA

component "**voice**\nits own UDP socket" as voice #E8F5E9
component "**files**\nsigned URL, out of band" as files #E8F5E9
component "**operator-api**\nREST + OpenAPI\n**off by default**" as opapi #EDE7F6

client --> gw : **control** · Mumble over TCP+TLS
gw --> svc : gRPC, routed by the\n**16-bit type in the frame header**

client --> voice : **realtime** · UDP, no hop
client --> files : **bulk** · HTTPS
oper --> opapi : **admin** · HTTPS, loopback

note right of gw
  Two facts carry the rest of the design.
  **Single writer per client socket**, so
  per-client ordering holds by construction.
  The wire type is in the **framing**, never
  in the protobuf, so routing is two bytes
  and a lookup.
  --
  So the gateway parses no payload, links no
  service's stubs, and never recompiles when
  a service is added.
  **A new service is a TOML block**, not a release.
end note

note bottom of voice
  `voice`, `files` and `operator-api` are three
  of the 21. They are drawn outside only because
  a client reaches them **without the gateway**,
  which is what this diagram is about.
end note

@enduml
